      "meaning": "The proof strengthens existing native walk contracts without changing their executable bodies. Reject makes the existing Black-recovery predicate false. The thin frame decode wrapper forwards to the actual unchanged decoder once, then composes its existing event contract; the public native result/progress predicates include recovered=false."
    },
    {
      "edge": "accepted mathematical MFr/canonical fold -> complete receiver relation",
      "meaning": "The accepted 2a-M definitions and totality certificate are unchanged. Native call history is used only to prove equality with the independently defined value, never to define it."
    },
    {
      "edge": "accepted source/data/ownership/M5 trace invariants -> establish -> strict_iterator_wf",
      "meaning": "Constructors and every completed public step derive the complete invariant without measuring future frame data. A partially failed private working canvas is not equated with a returned display canvas; the successful returned trace remains exact."
    },
    {
      "edge": "actual native result + actual appended canvas + raw selected controls -> call_complete",
      "meaning": "FrameView creation follows the checked equality proof and borrows the same canvas. Format, IEND and failed-Saved branches compose their actual transitions; OOM identity comes from the sealed failed log."
    },
    {
      "edge": "accepted cumulative requests/log and sticky history -> G_iter/Prog_ITER -> finite_progress/finite_fusion",
      "meaning": "The Saved threshold is inclusive at the first failing qualifying frame. Arbitrary finite-sequence induction excludes earlier OOM when the final cumulative log is all Ok, and fixes all later terminal results/logs/work after a terminal transition."
    },
    {
      "edge": "actual selection/reservation/disposal/decode/normalization/resume sites -> one sealed activity trace -> checked terminal zero counters",
      "meaning": "Only recording increments trace counters. The actual iterator threads one trace and snapshots it before every return; no-work is not inferred from identical results or logs. The companion source control pins the six site bindings and forwarding."
    }
